anaged  um  cryospark version so you wouldn't have  to deploy it yourself  well  just checking which if one of the other  colleagues wanted to um  steve  yeah i'm happy about that um actually  that's an ongoing discussion that's more  sort of directly uh related to sort of  the crowd spot folks but we we are  discussing that with them as well so  we'll follow up with you on that um but  really that's that's the the structure  by technology folks as well  wonderful thank you and i want to thank  all of you for your presentations today  this has been a wonderful presentation  would you like to provide any closing  remarks i'm not sure if all of you want  to or how about if i just allow um any  of you to just say anything if you'd  like to add before we close  i'll jump in and just talk about the  partnership between all of the aws  people and and thermo fisher and  astrazeneca i think  sometimes if you haven't never run  anything in the cloud  it can be a little bit overwhelming  seeing all of the technology and the  acronyms and the instance types and the  costs and  i just want to  reassure attendees that aws has  resources and people to help you with  that  we've worked very closely with thermo  fisher to make sure that  you know brian is obviously focusing on  the hpc side but working with thermo  fisher's i.t personnel making sure that  all of the networking and data transfer  is happening in a cost optimized and  secure way  we have a lot of best practices  resources that are publicly available  training that's publicly available demos  and videos that are publicly available  so you can start your learning journey  wherever you are  and start building with the skills that  you already have and kind of learn new  skills as you go  so yeah the  the success that we've seen on this  webinar has just been phenomenal and  it's been really great to  talk about the results and see um the  significant  acceleration of the science that's  happening at thermo fisher and  a